window.SOURATE_DATA = {"numSourate":38,"nomSourate":"Sad","nomFr":"Sad","nomEn":"The Letter \"Saad\"","nomArabe":"ص","lieu":"La Mecque","lieuEn":"Makkah","typeSourateLabel":"Sourate Mecquoise","typeSourateLabelEn":"Meccan Surah","typeSourateClasse":"mecquoise","ordreRev":38,"nbVersets":88,"versets":[{"numVerset":1,"texteArabe":"بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيمِ ص  وَالْقُرْآنِ ذِي الذِّكْرِ","tradPropre":"Sâd. Par le Coran, au renom glorieux (dikr)!","tradEn":"Ṣād. By the Qur’ān containing reminder...","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Şâd: Ces lettres isolées placées en ouverture de la sourate appartiennent au secret d'Allāh et démontrent le miracle inimitable du Coran, composé des mêmes lettres arabes que celles utilisées par les hommes. Je prête serment par le Coran qui contient un rappel au gens concernant leur vie dans le bas monde et dans l’au-delà, qu’il n’existe pas d’associés à Allah comme le prétendent les polythéistes.","explicationEn":"1. Saad. By the Qur’ān containing reminder. The discussion on similar letters has already passed in the beginning of Sūrah Al-Baqarah. I swear by the Qur’ān which is full of admonition, reminding mankind that which benefits them in their worldly life and the Afterlife. The matter is not as the idolaters think, namely that Allah has partners beside Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038001","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-182.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-2.html"},{"numVerset":2,"texteArabe":"بَلِ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا فِي عِزَّةٍ وَشِقَاقٍ","tradPropre":"Ceux qui ont mécru sont plutôt dans l'orgueil et le schisme!","tradEn":"But those who disbelieve are in pride and dissension.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Seulement, les mécréants refusent, par orgueil et par arrogance, de proclamer l’Unicité d’Allah et sont opposés et hostiles au Prophète Muħammad.","explicationEn":"2. But the disbelievers are in fanaticism and arrogance towards the oneness of Allah, and in opposition to Muhammad (peace be upon him) and hatred for him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038002","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-1.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-3.html"},{"numVerset":3,"texteArabe":"كَمْ أَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِنْ قَرْنٍ فَنَادَوْا وَلَاتَ حِينَ مَنَاصٍ","tradPropre":"Que de générations avant eux avons-Nous fait périr, qui ont crié, hélas, quand il n'était plus temps d'échapper?","tradEn":"How many a generation have We destroyed before them, and they [then] called out; but it was not a time for escape.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Que sont nombreuses les générations que Nous avons anéanties. Des générations qui traitaient de menteurs leurs messagers et qui ont crié au secours lorsque le châtiment s’est abattu sur eux. Or il était trop tard pour crier au secours et pour qu’on les épargne.","explicationEn":"3. How many generations who denied their messengers before them have I destroyed, they called out seeking help when the punishment fell upon them. But the time was not the time to be saved from the punishment where seeking help from Him would benefit them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038003","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-2.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-4.html"},{"numVerset":4,"texteArabe":"وَعَجِبُوا أَنْ جَاءَهُمْ مُنْذِرٌ مِنْهُمْ  وَقَالَ الْكَافِرُونَ هَاذَا سَاحِرٌ كَذَّابٌ","tradPropre":"Et ils (les Mecquois) s'étonnèrent qu'un avertisseur parmi eux leur soit venu, et les infidèles disent: «C'est un magicien et un grand menteur,","tradEn":"And they wonder that there has come to them a warner [i.e., Prophet Muḥammad (ﷺ)] from among themselves. And the disbelievers say, \"This is a magician and a liar.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils se sont étonnés qu’un Messager issu d’eux, les avertisse qu’un châtiment d’Allah leur était promis s’ils persistaient dans leur mécréance et les mécréants dirent lorsqu’ils virent les preuves de la véracité de ce qu’apportait le Prophète Muħammad: Cet homme est un sorcier qui ensorcelle les gens et un menteur qui prétend être un messager recevant la Révélation d’Allah.","explicationEn":"4. And they expressed surprise when a messenger came to them from themselves to warn them of Allah’s punishment if they remain in their disbelief. And the disbelievers said when they saw the proof for the truthfulness of what Muhammad (peace be upon him) brought: “This is a magician who performs magic on people, and a liar in claiming that he is a messenger from Allah who receives revelation.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038004","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-3.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-5.html"},{"numVerset":5,"texteArabe":"أَجَعَلَ الْآلِهَةَ إِلَاهًا وَاحِدًا  إِنَّ هَاذَا لَشَيْءٌ عُجَابٌ","tradPropre":"Réduira-t-il les divinités à un Seul Dieu? Voilà une chose vraiment étonnante».","tradEn":"Has he made the gods [only] one God? Indeed, this is a curious thing.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Cet homme réduit-il le nombre des divinités à un seul Dieu en dehors duquel il n’existe pas d’autres divinités? Ceci est vraiment stupéfiant.","explicationEn":"5. Has he made the numerous gods into one God, besides whom there is no god? This act of his is extremely strange”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038005","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-4.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-6.html"},{"numVerset":6,"texteArabe":"وَانْطَلَقَ الْمَلَأُ مِنْهُمْ أَنِ امْشُوا وَاصْبِرُوا عَلَىٰ آلِهَتِكُمْ  إِنَّ هَاذَا لَشَيْءٌ يُرَادُ","tradPropre":"Et leurs notables partirent en disant: «Allez-vous en, et restez constants à vos dieux: c'est là vraiment une chose souhaitable.","tradEn":"And the eminent among them went forth, [saying], \"Continue, and be patient over [the defense of] your gods. Indeed, this is a thing intended.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Obtenir le pouvoir et les honneurs, expliquent certains exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"Leurs nobles et leurs notables partirent en disant à leurs partisans: Restez fidèles à votre confession et n’embrassez pas la religion de Muħammad. Restez fermement attachés à l’adoration de vos divinités car l’adoration d’un seul Dieu à laquelle vous appelle Muħammad est un stratagème qu’il a ourdi afin qu’il nous domine et que nous lui soyons assujettis.","explicationEn":"6. And their leaders and elders went, saying to their followers: “Carry on with what you are upon and do not enter the religion of Muhammad. Remain firm on worshipping your gods. That which Muhammad is calling you towards, namely worshipping one god, is something planned which he wants so that he can dominate over us and have followers for himself.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038006","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-5.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-7.html"},{"numVerset":7,"texteArabe":"مَا سَمِعْنَا بِهَاذَا فِي الْمِلَّةِ الْآخِرَةِ إِنْ هَاذَا إِلَّا اخْتِلَاقٌ","tradPropre":"Nous n'avons pas entendu cela dans la dernière religion (le Christianisme); ce n'est en vérité que pure invention!","tradEn":"We have not heard of this in the latest religion. This is not but a fabrication.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous n’avons pas entendu parler du monothéisme auquel nous appelle Muħammad ni chez nos aïeux ni dans la religion de Jésus. Il ne fait que proférer des mensonges et des inventions.","explicationEn":"7. We have not heard the oneness of Allah which Muhammad is calling us towards in what we found our fathers on nor in the religion of Jesus (peace be upon him). What we have heard from him is nothing but a lie and fabrication.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038007","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-6.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-8.html"},{"numVerset":8,"texteArabe":"أَأُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ الذِّكْرُ مِنْ بَيْنِنَا  بَلْ هُمْ فِي شَكٍّ مِنْ ذِكْرِي  بَلْ لَمَّا يَذُوقُوا عَذَابِ","tradPropre":"Quoi! C'est sur lui, parmi nous, qu'on aurait fait descendre le Rappel [le Coran]?» Plutôt ils sont dans le doute au sujet de Mon message. Ou plutôt ils n'ont pas encore goûté à Mon châtiment!","tradEn":"Has the message been revealed to him out of [all of] us?\" Rather, they are in doubt about My message. Rather, they have not yet tasted My punishment.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Est-il concevable que le Coran lui soit révélé à lui parmi nous tous et qu’il soit privilégié alors que nous sommes des chefs et des notables? Ces polythéistes douteront de la Révélation tant qu’ils n’auront pas goûté au châtiment d’Allah et ils sont trompés par le délai que Nous leur accordons. S’ils goûtaient au châtiment, ils n’oseraient pas se rendre coupables de mécréance et de polythéisme ni n’oseraient douter de ce qui t’est révélé.","explicationEn":"8. Is it right that the Qur’ān is revealed to him from amongst us and he is chosen for it, and it is not revealed to us whereas we are great leaders?” But these idolaters are in doubt about the revelation which is revealed to you. And they have not yet tasted the punishment of Allah, so they have been deceived due to their being given respite. If they were to taste it, they would not have the audacity to disbelieve in Allah and doubt what is revealed to you.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038008","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-7.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-9.html"},{"numVerset":9,"texteArabe":"أَمْ عِنْدَهُمْ خَزَائِنُ رَحْمَةِ رَبِّكَ الْعَزِيزِ الْوَهَّابِ","tradPropre":"Ou bien détiennent-ils les trésors de la miséricorde de ton Seigneur, le Puissant, le Dispensateur par excellence.","tradEn":"Or do they have the depositories of the mercy of your Lord, the Exalted in Might, the Bestower?","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Pour décider qui doit être choisi comme prophète. Ce verset est donc une réponse au verset précédent.","explicationUnanime":"Ces polythéistes dénégateurs détiennent-ils les réserves de la grâce de ton Puissant Seigneur à qui personne ne tient tête, Celui qui donne ce qu’Il veut à qui Il veut? L’une des grâces issues de Sa réserve, est la Prophétie qu’Il donne à qui Il veut et il ne leur appartient pas de prétendre l’accorder à qui ils veulent et en priver qui ils veulent.","explicationEn":"9. Or do these denying idolaters have treasures of the grace of your Lord, the Mighty whom nobody can overpower, who gives what He wants to whom He wants? And from His treasures is prophethood, so He gives it to whom He wishes. It is not for them that they should give it to whom they want and stop it from whom they want.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038009","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-8.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-10.html"},{"numVerset":10,"texteArabe":"أَمْ لَهُمْ مُلْكُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا  فَلْيَرْتَقُوا فِي الْأَسْبَابِ","tradPropre":"Ou bien ont-ils le royaume des cieux et de la terre et de ce qui existe entre eux? Eh bien, qu'ils y montent par n'importe quel moyen!","tradEn":"Or is theirs the dominion of the heavens and the earth and what is between them? Then let them ascend through [any] ways of access.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Détiennent-ils la propriété des Cieux, de la Terre et de ce qu’ils contiennent? Ont-ils le droit de donner et de ne pas donner? Si c’est ce qu’ils prétendent, qu’ils se donnent donc les moyens d’atteindre le ciel afin qu’ils puissent donner et ne pas donner comme bon leur semble, mais ils n’en seront jamais capables.","explicationEn":"10. Or do they have the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, and possession of everything therein so they may chose who to give it to? If this is what claim they are making then let them adopt the means to go up to the heavens so they can then rule how they wish from above the heavens in who should be given and who should be held back from.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038010","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-9.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-11.html"},{"numVerset":11,"texteArabe":"جُنْدٌ مَا هُنَالِكَ مَهْزُومٌ مِنَ الْأَحْزَابِ","tradPropre":"Une armée de coalisés qui, ici-même, sera mise en déroute!","tradEn":"[They are but] soldiers [who will be] defeated there among the companies [of disbelievers].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces gens qui traitent Muħammad de menteur seront des soldats vaincus comme les soldats qui les ont précédés et ont traité de menteurs leurs messagers.","explicationEn":"11. These deniers of Muhammad (peace be upon him) are a defeated army like the armies which came before them who denied their messengers and so I destroyed them. So that will occur with this army as occurred with others.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038011","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-10.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-12.html"},{"numVerset":12,"texteArabe":"كَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوحٍ وَعَادٌ وَفِرْعَوْنُ ذُو الْأَوْتَادِ","tradPropre":"Avant eux, le peuple de Noé, les Aad et Pharaon l'homme aux pals (ou aux Pyramides),","tradEn":"The people of Noah denied before them, and [the tribe of] ʿAad and Pharaoh, the owner of stakes,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils ne sont pas les premiers de leur genre puisqu’ils ont été précédés par le peuple de Noé, les ‘Âd et Pharaon qui faisait subir aux gens le supplice du pal.","explicationEn":"12. These deniers are not the first to deny, because the people of Noah, Aad, and the powerful Pharaoh denied before them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038012","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-11.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-13.html"},{"numVerset":13,"texteArabe":"وَثَمُودُ وَقَوْمُ لُوطٍ وَأَصْحَابُ الْأَيْكَةِ  أُولَائِكَ الْأَحْزَابُ","tradPropre":"et les Tamûd, le peuple de Lot, et les gens d'Al-Aykah, (ont tous démenti leurs Messagers). Voilà les coalisés.","tradEn":"And [the tribe of] Thamūd and the people of Lot and the companions of the thicket [i.e., people of Madyan]. Those are the companies.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils ont aussi été précédés par les Thâmûd, le peuple de Loth et le peuple de Chu’ayb. Ce sont eux les coalisés qui se sont unis contre leurs messagers afin de les traiter de menteurs et de mécroire en ce qu’ils apportaient.","explicationEn":"13. And Thamud, the people of Lot and the people of Shu’ayb denied. Those are the groups who were all united in their denial of the messengers and disbelief of what they brought.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038013","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-12.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-14.html"},{"numVerset":14,"texteArabe":"إِنْ كُلٌّ إِلَّا كَذَّبَ الرُّسُلَ فَحَقَّ عِقَابِ","tradPropre":"Il n'en est aucun qui n'ait traité les Messagers de menteurs. Et bien, Ma punition s'est avérée contre eux!","tradEn":"Each of them denied the messengers, so My penalty was justified.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Aucun de ces coalisés ne s'est épargné de traiter ses messagers de menteurs. Ils méritaient donc le châtiment d’Allah et ils furent punis, même si parfois ce ne fut pas immédiatement.","explicationEn":"14. There is not a single one of these groups except that it denied the messengers. So Allah’s punishment was justified for them and His punishment befell them, even though it was delayed for a while.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038014","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-13.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-15.html"},{"numVerset":15,"texteArabe":"وَمَا يَنْظُرُ هَاؤُلَاءِ إِلَّا صَيْحَةً وَاحِدَةً مَا لَهَا مِنْ فَوَاقٍ","tradPropre":"Ceux-ci n'attendant qu'un seul Cri, sans répétition.","tradEn":"And these [disbelievers] await not but one blast [of the Horn]; for it there will be no delay.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ou : différé, ou encore : qui n’aura pas besoin d’être répété.","explicationUnanime":"Ces gens qui traitent Muħammad de menteur n’attendent que le second et dernier souffle dans la Trompe et que le châtiment s’abatte sur eux, s’ils meurent pendant qu’ils persistent à le traiter de menteur.","explicationEn":"15. These deniers of Muhammad (peace be upon him) are not waiting except for the second blowing of the Trumpet in which there shall be no return. Then the punishment will fall upon them if they had died in a state of denial.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038015","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-14.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-16.html"},{"numVerset":16,"texteArabe":"وَقَالُوا رَبَّنَا عَجِّلْ لَنَا قِطَّنَا قَبْلَ يَوْمِ الْحِسَابِ","tradPropre":"Et ils disent: «Seigneur, hâte-nous notre part avant le jour des Comptes».","tradEn":"And they say, \"Our Lord, hasten for us our share [of the punishment] before the Day of Account.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ou : montre-nous dès maintenant le registre de nos œuvres.","explicationUnanime":"Ils dirent d’un ton railleur: Ô notre Seigneur, avance donc notre part de châtiment dans le bas monde avant l’au-delà.","explicationEn":"16. And they said mockingly: “Our Lord, give us our share of punishment in the worldly life before the day of judgment”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038016","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-15.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-17.html"},{"numVerset":17,"texteArabe":"اصْبِرْ عَلَىٰ مَا يَقُولُونَ وَاذْكُرْ عَبْدَنَا دَاوُودَ ذَا الْأَيْدِ  إِنَّهُ أَوَّابٌ","tradPropre":"Endure ce qu'ils disent; et rappelle-toi David, Notre serviteur, doué de force [dans l'adoration] et plein de repentir [à Allah].","tradEn":"Be patient over what they say and remember Our servant, David, the possessor of strength; indeed, he was one who repeatedly turned back [to Allāh].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, endure les paroles désagréables que profèrent ces dénégateurs et rappelle-toi Notre serviteur David doué d’une grande force qui lui permettait de combattre ses ennemis et d’être endurant dans son obéissance à Allah. Il se repentait souvent à Allah et œuvrait de manière à mériter Son agrément.","explicationEn":"17. O Messenger, be patient on the things these deniers say which do not please you, and remember My servant David, who had the power to fight his enemies and persevere in Allah’s obedience. He used to turn to Allah frequently through repentance and actions which please Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038017","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-16.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-18.html"},{"numVerset":18,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا سَخَّرْنَا الْجِبَالَ مَعَهُ يُسَبِّحْنَ بِالْعَشِيِّ وَالْإِشْرَاقِ","tradPropre":"Nous soumîmes les montagnes à glorifier Allah, soir et matin, en sa compagnie,","tradEn":"Indeed, We subjected the mountains [to praise] with him, exalting [Allāh] in the [late] afternoon and [after] sunrise.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons assujetti les montagnes afin qu’elles glorifient Allah de concert avec David en début et en fin de journée.","explicationEn":"18. I subjugated the mountains with David. They would exalt with his exalting at the end of the day and its beginning at sunrise.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038018","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-17.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-19.html"},{"numVerset":19,"texteArabe":"وَالطَّيْرَ مَحْشُورَةً  كُلٌّ لَهُ أَوَّابٌ","tradPropre":"de même que les oiseaux assemblés en masse, tous ne faisant qu'obéir à lui [Allah].","tradEn":"And the birds were assembled, all with him repeating [praises].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons également assujetti les oiseaux en suspens dans les airs et tous Le glorifient et se repentent à Lui.","explicationEn":"19. And I subjugated the birds held in the air. Each of them was obedient, exalting out of following him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038019","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-18.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-20.html"},{"numVerset":20,"texteArabe":"وَشَدَدْنَا مُلْكَهُ وَآتَيْنَاهُ الْحِكْمَةَ وَفَصْلَ الْخِطَابِ","tradPropre":"Et Nous renforçâmes son royaume et lui donnâmes la sagesse et la faculté de bien juger.","tradEn":"And We strengthened his kingdom and gave him wisdom and discernment in speech.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous rendîmes son royaume plus puissant par le prestige, la force et la domination que Nous lui avons accordés sur ses ennemis. Nous lui avons aussi fait don de la Prophétie, la sagesse dans la prise de décision, la faculté d’exprimer tout ce qu’il désire, et la pertinence dans le jugement.","explicationEn":"20. And I strengthened his kingdom through the awe, strength and help against his enemies I had given him. And I gave him prophethood and correctness in his affairs. And I gave him clear eloquence in every objective, and decisiveness in speech and wisdom.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038020","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-19.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-21.html"},{"numVerset":21,"texteArabe":"۞ وَهَلْ أَتَاكَ نَبَأُ الْخَصْمِ إِذْ تَسَوَّرُوا الْمِحْرَابَ","tradPropre":"Et t'est-elle parvenue la nouvelle des disputeurs quand ils grimpèrent au mur du sanctuaire!","tradEn":"And has there come to you the news of the adversaries, when they climbed over the wall of [his] prayer chamber -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, la nouvelle des deux antagonistes qui escaladèrent le mur du sanctuaire de David t’est-elle parvenue?","explicationEn":"21. O Messenger, has the news of the two disputants come to you, when they climbed upon the place of worship of David (peace be upon him)?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038021","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-22.html"},{"numVerset":22,"texteArabe":"إِذْ دَخَلُوا عَلَىٰ دَاوُودَ فَفَزِعَ مِنْهُمْ  قَالُوا لَا تَخَفْ  خَصْمَانِ بَغَىٰ بَعْضُنَا عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ فَاحْكُمْ بَيْنَنَا بِالْحَقِّ وَلَا تُشْطِطْ وَاهْدِنَا إِلَىٰ سَوَاءِ الصِّرَاطِ","tradPropre":"Quand ils entrèrent auprès de David, il en fut effrayé. Ils dirent: «N'aie pas peur! Nous sommes tous deux en dispute; l'un de nous a fait du tort à l'autre. Juge donc en toute équité entre nous, ne sois pas injuste et guide-nous vers le chemin droit.","tradEn":"When they entered upon David and he was alarmed by them? They said, \"Fear not. [We are] two adversaries, one of whom has wronged the other, so judge between us with truth and do not exceed [it] and guide us to the sound path.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils entrèrent soudainement auprès de lui et il fut pris de frayeur par cette intrusion. Lorsqu’ils virent sa réaction, ils lui dirent: Ne crains rien, nous sommes deux antagonistes et l’un de nous a commis une injustice envers l’autre. Juge entre nous avec équité, ne sois pas injuste et oriente-nous vers le droit chemin.","explicationEn":"22. When they entered upon David suddenly, so he became frightened due to their strange act of entering upon him in this most unusual of ways. When they saw his fear, they said: “Do not fear. We are two disputants, one of us having wronged the other, so judge between us justly and do not be unjust when you judge between us, and guide us to the right path which is the path of correctness”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038022","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-21.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-23.html"},{"numVerset":23,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ هَاذَا أَخِي لَهُ تِسْعٌ وَتِسْعُونَ نَعْجَةً وَلِيَ نَعْجَةٌ وَاحِدَةٌ فَقَالَ أَكْفِلْنِيهَا وَعَزَّنِي فِي الْخِطَابِ","tradPropre":"Celui-ci est mon frère: il a quatre-vingt-dix-neuf brebis, tandis que je n'ai qu'une brebis. Il m'a dit: «Confie-la-moi» et dans la conversation, il a beaucoup fait pression sur moi».","tradEn":"Indeed this, my brother, has ninety-nine ewes, and I have one ewe; so he said, 'Entrust her to me,' and he overpowered me in speech.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"L’un des deux antagonistes dit à David: Cet homme est mon frère. Il possède quatre-vingt-dix-neuf brebis et j’en possède une. Il me demanda de lui donner la mienne et a fait preuve de grande persuasion.","explicationEn":"23. One of the disputants said to David (peace be upon him): “This man is my brother. He has ninety-nine ewes and I have one ewe. He asked me to give him that too and he has overpowered me in proof”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038023","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-22.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-24.html"},{"numVerset":24,"texteArabe":"قَالَ لَقَدْ ظَلَمَكَ بِسُؤَالِ نَعْجَتِكَ إِلَىٰ نِعَاجِهِ  وَإِنَّ كَثِيرًا مِنَ الْخُلَطَاءِ لَيَبْغِي بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ إِلَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ وَقَلِيلٌ مَا هُمْ  وَظَنَّ دَاوُودُ أَنَّمَا فَتَنَّاهُ فَاسْتَغْفَرَ رَبَّهُ وَخَرَّ رَاكِعًا وَأَنَابَ ۩","tradPropre":"Il [David] dit: «Il a été certes injuste envers toi en demandant de joindre ta brebis à ses brebis». Beaucoup de gens transgressent les droits de leurs associés, sauf ceux qui croient et accomplissent les bonnes œuvres - cependant ils sont bien rares -. Et David pensa alors que Nous l'avions mis à l'épreuve. Il demanda donc pardon à son Seigneur et tomba prosterné et se repentit.","tradEn":"[David] said, \"He has certainly wronged you in demanding your ewe [in addition] to his ewes. And indeed, many associates oppress one another, except for those who believe and do righteous deeds - and few are they.\" And David became certain that We had tried him, and he asked forgiveness of his Lord and fell down bowing [in prostration] and turned in repentance [to Allāh].","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Les associés, selon la majorité des commentateurs.<br><br><strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> De nombreux exégètes mentionnent au niveau de ce récit tout ou partie d’une histoire tirée de l’Ancien Testament - dont le croyant est en droit de douter - selon laquelle David, qui disposait déjà d’un grand nombre de femmes, aurait convoité l’épouse de l’un de ses lieutenants qu’il aurait même envoyé se faire tuer au combat afin de pouvoir l’épouser. L’irruption des deux plaideurs dans son oratoire aurait donc eu pour seul objectif de lui faire prendre conscience de son erreur, la brebis symbolisant ici la femme. Toutefois, si ce récit fait bien allusion à cet épisode, les termes du Coran indiquent seulement que David a été blâmé pour avoir demandé à cet homme de répudier sa femme afin de pouvoir l’épouser ou de se désister en sa faveur, si le mariage n’avait pas encore été célébré. On est donc loin des péchés que la Bible attribue à David et à d’autres prophètes qui, selon le Coran, sont les êtres les plus vertueux, si bien que, s’il leur arrive de commettre une faute vénielle, ils s’empressent de s’en repentir. C’est le cas notamment d’Adam qui, selon le Coran, s’est repenti de sa faute, tandis que les chrétiens - et non la Bible - font du péché originel, justifiant la Rédemption par la crucifixion du Christ, le fondement de leur religion.","explicationUnanime":"David émit son jugement et s’adressa au plaignant en ces termes: Ton frère a certainement été injuste envers toi lorsqu’il t’a demandé de lui donner ta brebis pour l’ajouter aux siennes. Nombreux sont ceux qui violent les droits de leurs associés, excepté les croyants qui accomplissent de bonnes œuvres. Eux ne lèsent pas leurs associés, mais ils sont peu nombreux. David s’aperçut ensuite que Nous l’avions éprouvé par cette querelle et il demanda alors pardon à son Seigneur, se prosterna afin de se rapprocher de Lui et se repentit à Lui. Ceci est une parabole énoncée parAllah, faisant référence à ce qui arriva à David avec la femme qui sollicita son jugement.","explicationEn":"24. Then David judged between them and addressed the claimant, saying: “Your brother has wronged you when he asked you to add your ewe to his ewes. And many partners oppress one another by taking their rights and not being fair, except the believers who do good actions, for they are fair with their partners and do not wrong them. But those attributed with that are few”. And David (peace be upon him) was convinced that I only put him to test through this dispute, so he sought forgiveness from his Lord and prostrated to get close to Him, and repented to Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038024","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-23.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-25.html"},{"numVerset":25,"texteArabe":"فَغَفَرْنَا لَهُ ذَالِكَ  وَإِنَّ لَهُ عِنْدَنَا لَزُلْفَىٰ وَحُسْنَ مَآبٍ","tradPropre":"Nous lui pardonnâmes. Il aura une place proche de Nous et un beau refuge.","tradEn":"So We forgave him that; and indeed, for him is nearness to Us and a good place of return.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous l’exauçâmes et lui pardonnâmes. Il est du nombre de ceux qui sont rapprochés de Nous et qui connaîtront un sort favorable dans l’au-delà.","explicationEn":"25. So I responded to him and forgave him that. And he is amongst the close ones with Me, and for him is a good return in the Afterlife.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038025","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-24.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-26.html"},{"numVerset":26,"texteArabe":"يَا دَاوُودُ إِنَّا جَعَلْنَاكَ خَلِيفَةً فِي الْأَرْضِ فَاحْكُمْ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ بِالْحَقِّ وَلَا تَتَّبِعِ الْهَوَىٰ فَيُضِلَّكَ عَنْ سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ  إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَضِلُّونَ عَنْ سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ شَدِيدٌ بِمَا نَسُوا يَوْمَ الْحِسَابِ","tradPropre":"«O David, Nous avons fait de toi un calife sur la terre. Juge donc en toute équité parmi les gens et ne suis pas la passion: sinon elle t'égarera du sentier d'Allah». Car ceux qui s'égarent du sentier d'Allah auront un dur châtiment pour avoir oublié le Jour des Comptes.","tradEn":"[We said], \"O David, indeed We have made you a successor upon the earth, so judge between the people in truth and do not follow [your own] desire, as it will lead you astray from the way of Allāh.\" Indeed, those who go astray from the way of Allāh will have a severe punishment for having forgotten the Day of Account.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô David, Nous avons fait de toi un successeur sur Terre qui exécute les jugements qui tranchent les affaires terrestres ou religieuses. Juge donc entre les gens avec équité et ne suis pas ta passion, en favorisant par exemple un des antagonistes en raison d’une proximité amicale ou familiale ou au contraire en le lésant en raison d’une animosité. La passion t’égarerait alors du droit chemin. Ceux qui s’égarent du droit chemin d’Allah subiront un châtiment sévère pour leur oubli du Jour du Jugement, s’ils l’avaient eu en mémoire et l’avaient redouté, ils n’auraient pas suivi leurs penchants.","explicationEn":"26. O David, I made you a deputy on earth to execute worldly and religious rulings and judgments, so judge between people with justice. And do not follow desires in your judgement between people, by inclining towards one of the disputants due to relationship or friendship, or by turning away from him due to enmity, whereby desires will misguide you from Allah’s straight path. Those who go astray from Allah’s straight path will have a severe punishment due to their forgetting the day of reckoning, because if they were to remember it and fear it they would not incline to their desires.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038026","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-25.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-27.html"},{"numVerset":27,"texteArabe":"وَمَا خَلَقْنَا السَّمَاءَ وَالْأَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا بَاطِلًا  ذَالِكَ ظَنُّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا  فَوَيْلٌ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِنَ النَّارِ","tradPropre":"Nous n'avons pas créé le ciel et la terre et ce qui existe entre eux en vain. C'est ce que pensent ceux qui ont mécru. Malheur à ceux qui ont mécru pour le feu [qui les attend]!","tradEn":"And We did not create the heaven and the earth and that between them aimlessly. That is the assumption of those who disbelieve, so woe to those who disbelieve from the Fire.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous n’avons pas créé le Ciel et la Terre vainement. C'est ce que pensent ceux qui ont mécru. Malheur donc à eux pour le châtiment du feu qui les attend le Jour de la Résurrection s’ils meurent mécréants et entretenant un mauvais soupçon à l’égard d’Allah.","explicationEn":"27. And I did not create the heavens or the earth in vain, but rather I created them out of complete wisdom to prove the power of Allah and so that He is obeyed in them. That is the belief of those who deny the truth who believe they were created in vain. So woe to these disbelievers who believe this from the fire of hell on the Day of Judgment, when they die on the disbelief and bad opinion of Allah they are upon.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038027","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-26.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-28.html"},{"numVerset":28,"texteArabe":"أَمْ نَجْعَلُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ كَالْمُفْسِدِينَ فِي الْأَرْضِ أَمْ نَجْعَلُ الْمُتَّقِينَ كَالْفُجَّارِ","tradPropre":"Traiterons-Nous ceux qui croient et accomplissent les bonnes œuvres comme ceux qui commettent du désordre sur terre? ou traiterons-Nous les pieux comme les pervers?","tradEn":"Or should We treat those who believe and do righteous deeds like corrupters in the land? Or should We treat those who fear Allāh like the wicked?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous ne mettrons pas sur un même pied d’égalité ceux qui croient en Allah, suivent Son Messager et accomplissent de bonnes œuvres et ceux qui, par leur mécréance et leurs péchés, commettent du désordre sur terre. Nous ne mettrons pas non plus sur un même pied d’égalité ceux qui craignent leur Seigneur en se conformant à Ses commandements et en renonçant à Ses interdits et les hypocrites qui se complaisent dans les actes de désobéissance. Les considérer comme égaux est une injustice qu'il ne sied pas à Allah de commettre. Au contraire, Allah rétribuera plutôt les croyants pieux en les faisant entrer au Paradis et punira les mécréants misérables en les faisant entrer en Enfer. Comme les deux partis ne sont pas égaux pour Allah, leur rétribution n’est pas égale pour Lui non plus.","explicationEn":"28. I will never make those who believe in Allah, follow His messenger and do good deeds like those who make the corruption on earth through disbelief and sins, nor will I make those who are mindful of their Lord by carrying out His orders and refraining from His prohibitions like the disbelievers and hypocrites who are engrossed in sins. Making them both equal is an injustice which does not befit Allah. But rather Allah will reward the pious believers by entry into Paradise and punish the wretched disbelievers by entry into the fire, because they are not equal in Allah’s sight so their reward is not equal in His sight too.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038028","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-27.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-29.html"},{"numVerset":29,"texteArabe":"كِتَابٌ أَنْزَلْنَاهُ إِلَيْكَ مُبَارَكٌ لِيَدَّبَّرُوا آيَاتِهِ وَلِيَتَذَكَّرَ أُولُو الْأَلْبَابِ","tradPropre":"[Voici] un Livre béni que Nous avons fait descendre vers toi, afin qu'ils méditent sur ses versets et que les doués d'intelligence réfléchissent!","tradEn":"[This is] a blessed Book which We have revealed to you, [O Muḥammad], that they might reflect upon its verses and that those of understanding would be reminded.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce Coran est un Livre que Nous t’avons révélé. Il contient de nombreux récits ainsi qu’une multitude de prescriptions utiles, afin que les gens méditent ses versets et réfléchissent sur leur sens et que les personnes douées d’une raison éclairée en tirent des enseignements.","explicationEn":"29. This Qur’ān is a book I revealed to you, O Prophet, abundant in good and benefit. I revealed it so that people ponder over its verses and contemplate its meanings, and so that the people of enlightened superior intellect take lessons from it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038029","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-28.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-30.html"},{"numVerset":30,"texteArabe":"وَوَهَبْنَا لِدَاوُودَ سُلَيْمَانَ  نِعْمَ الْعَبْدُ  إِنَّهُ أَوَّابٌ","tradPropre":"Et à David Nous fîmes don de Salomon, - quel bon serviteur! - Il était plein de repentir.","tradEn":"And to David We gave Solomon. An excellent servant, indeed he was one repeatedly turning back [to Allāh].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons donné Salomon comme fils à David, en guise de faveur de notre part, afin qu’il y trouve de la quiétude. Quel bon serviteur que Salomon: il se repentait souvent à Allah et s’en remettait à Lui.","explicationEn":"30. And I granted David his son Solomon, as a favour from Me to him and a grace so that he is pleased. What an excellent servant Solomon was. He would abundantly repent and turn to Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038030","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-29.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-31.html"},{"numVerset":31,"texteArabe":"إِذْ عُرِضَ عَلَيْهِ بِالْعَشِيِّ الصَّافِنَاتُ الْجِيَادُ","tradPropre":"Quand un après-midi, on lui présenta de magnifiques chevaux de course,","tradEn":"[Mention] when there were exhibited before him in the afternoon the poised [standing] racehorses.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Il s’agit, selon les commentateurs, de chevaux qui se tiennent sur trois pattes et le bout du sabot de la quatrième, signe d’élégance et de légèreté.","explicationUnanime":"Rappelle-toi lorsqu’on lui présenta un après-midi des pur-sang de course qui se tiennent debout sur trois pattes et lèvent la quatrième. On ne cessa de lui en présenter jusqu’à ce que le soleil se soit couché.","explicationEn":"31. Remember when at the time of Asr purebred fast horses were presented to him, standing on three feet with one foot raised. These purebred horses continued to be presented to him until sunset.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038031","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-30.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-32.html"},{"numVerset":32,"texteArabe":"فَقَالَ إِنِّي أَحْبَبْتُ حُبَّ الْخَيْرِ عَنْ ذِكْرِ رَبِّي حَتَّىٰ تَوَارَتْ بِالْحِجَابِ","tradPropre":"il dit: «Oui, je me suis complu à aimer les biens (de ce monde) au point [d'oublier] le rappel de mon Seigneur jusqu'à ce que [le soleil] se soit caché derrière son voile.","tradEn":"And he said, \"Indeed, I gave preference to the love of good [things] over the remembrance of my Lord until it [i.e., the sun] disappeared into the curtain [of darkness].\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> De la prière, précisent nombre de commentateurs.","explicationUnanime":"Salomon dit: J’ai préféré mon amour des biens de ce monde, dont font partie les chevaux, à l’évocation de mon Seigneur au point que le soleil s’est couché et que j’ai manqué la prière de l’après-midi.","explicationEn":"32. So Solomon said: “I preferred love of wealth, these horses being part of it, over the remembrance of my Lord until the sun set.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038032","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-31.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-33.html"},{"numVerset":33,"texteArabe":"رُدُّوهَا عَلَيَّ  فَطَفِقَ مَسْحًا بِالسُّوقِ وَالْأَعْنَاقِ","tradPropre":"Ramenez-les moi.» Alors il se mit à leur couper les pattes et les cous.","tradEn":"[He said], \"Return them to me,\" and set about striking [their] legs and necks.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Approchez de moi ces chevaux, ordonna-t-il et on les approcha de lui. Puis il se mit à les frapper au cou et aux pattes avec son sabre.","explicationEn":"33. Return these horses to me”. So they returned them to him, then he began striking their legs and necks with his sword.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038033","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-32.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-34.html"},{"numVerset":34,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ فَتَنَّا سُلَيْمَانَ وَأَلْقَيْنَا عَلَىٰ كُرْسِيِّهِ جَسَدًا ثُمَّ أَنَابَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous avions certes éprouvé Salomon en plaçant sur son siège un corps. Ensuite, il se repentit.","tradEn":"And We certainly tried Solomon and placed on his throne a body; then he returned.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> La nature de ce corps a donné lieu à diverses interprétations. L’on retient de ce verset, et c’est l’essentiel, que Salomon, comme son père David, fut éprouvé par son Seigneur qui accepta finalement son repentir.","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons éprouvé Salomon et avons placé sur son trône un démon ayant une apparence humaine qui régna une courte période sur son royaume, puis Salomon récupéra son royaume et son ascendant sur les démons.","explicationEn":"34. And I tested Solomon and put on his chair part of a child, and that was when he swore by Allah that he will sleep with all of his wives and each one of them will bring forth a horseman to strive in Allah’s way. But he did not say in this oath of his: “if Allah wills”. So he slept with all of them, but none of them gave birth except one who gave birth to part of a child. Then Solomon repented to his Lord.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038034","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-33.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-35.html"},{"numVerset":35,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِي وَهَبْ لِي مُلْكًا لَا يَنْبَغِي لِأَحَدٍ مِنْ بَعْدِي  إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْوَهَّابُ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Seigneur, pardonne-moi et fais-moi don d'un royaume tel que nul après moi n'aura de pareil. C'est Toi le grand Dispensateur».","tradEn":"He said, \"My Lord, forgive me and grant me a kingdom such as will not belong to anyone after me. Indeed, You are the Bestower.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Salomon dit: Ô Seigneur, pardonne-moi mes péchés et accorde-moi un royaume qui m’est spécifique et que personne n’aura après moi. Ô Seigneur, c’est Toi qui dispenses ce que Tu veux.","explicationEn":"35. Solomon said: “My Lord, forgive me my sins and grant me a kingdom especially for me which no person will have after me. My Lord, You give abundantly and are very generous”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038035","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-34.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-36.html"},{"numVerset":36,"texteArabe":"فَسَخَّرْنَا لَهُ الرِّيحَ تَجْرِي بِأَمْرِهِ رُخَاءً حَيْثُ أَصَابَ","tradPropre":"Nous lui assujettîmes alors le vent qui, par son ordre, soufflait modérément partout où il voulait.","tradEn":"So We subjected to him the wind blowing by his command, gently, wherever he directed,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous l’exauçâmes alors et lui avons assujetti le vent qui soufflait doucement par son ordre, malgré sa force et sa vitesse, et le transportait où il le voulait.","explicationEn":"36. So I responded to him and made the wind subservient to him. It would obey his order, gently. There was no shaking in it, despite its strength and its fast movement. It would carry him wherever he wanted.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038036","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-35.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-37.html"},{"numVerset":37,"texteArabe":"وَالشَّيَاطِينَ كُلَّ بَنَّاءٍ وَغَوَّاصٍ","tradPropre":"De même que les diables, bâtisseurs et plongeurs de toutes sortes.","tradEn":"And [also] the devils [of jinn] - every builder and diver","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous lui avons également assujetti les démons qui suivaient ses ordres à la lettre: certains étaient des bâtisseurs et d’autres des plongeurs qui s’introduisaient profondément sous la mer pour en extraire des perles.","explicationEn":"37. And I made the satans subservient to him, complying with his orders. Some of them were builders and others were divers who would dive into the seas and take out pearls from them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038037","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-36.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-38.html"},{"numVerset":38,"texteArabe":"وَآخَرِينَ مُقَرَّنِينَ فِي الْأَصْفَادِ","tradPropre":"Et d'autres encore, accouplés dans des chaînes.","tradEn":"And others bound together in irons.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il y a avait aussi parmi les démons qui lui étaient assujettis, des démons rebelles enchaînés incapables de se mouvoir avec liberté.","explicationEn":"38. And from the satans there were rebellious ones who were made subservient for him. They were tied up in shackles, unable to move.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038038","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-37.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-39.html"},{"numVerset":39,"texteArabe":"هَاذَا عَطَاؤُنَا فَامْنُنْ أَوْ أَمْسِكْ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ","tradPropre":"«Voilà Notre don; distribue-le ou retiens-le sans avoir à en rendre compte».","tradEn":"[We said], \"This is Our gift, so grant or withhold without account.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Salomon, voici le don que Nous t’avons fait en guise de réponse à ce que tu Nous as demandé. Donnes-en à qui tu veux et prives-en qui tu veux, tu n’auras aucun compte à rendre à ce sujet.","explicationEn":"39. “O Solomon, this is My gift which I granted you in response to what you asked of Me. So give whom you want and stop from whom you want, as I will not take you to account in your giving or holding back”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038039","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-38.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-40.html"},{"numVerset":40,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ لَهُ عِنْدَنَا لَزُلْفَىٰ وَحُسْنَ مَآبٍ","tradPropre":"Et il a une place rapprochée de Nous et un beau refuge.","tradEn":"And indeed, for him is nearness to Us and a good place of return.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Salomon est pour Nous du nombre des rapprochés et il habitera dans une demeure agréable lorsqu’il retournera auprès de Nous. Cette demeure est le Paradis.","explicationEn":"40. And Solomon is amongst the close ones with us, and he has a good return which he will return to, and it is Paradise.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038040","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-39.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-41.html"},{"numVerset":41,"texteArabe":"وَاذْكُرْ عَبْدَنَا أَيُّوبَ إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُ أَنِّي مَسَّنِيَ الشَّيْطَانُ بِنُصْبٍ وَعَذَابٍ","tradPropre":"Et rappelle-toi Job, Notre serviteur, lorsqu'il appela son Seigneur: «Le Diable m'a infligé détresse et souffrance».","tradEn":"And remember Our servant Job, when he called to his Lord, \"Indeed, Satan has touched me with hardship and torment.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Les souffrances de la maladie et les tourments causés par la disparition de ses richesses et de ses enfants.","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, rappelle-toi de Notre serviteur Job qui dit en invoquant Allah: Satan m’a infligé un mal et une peine douloureuse.","explicationEn":"41. O Messenger, remember My servant Job when he called upon Allah, his Lord: “The satan has afflicted Me with a tiring and tormentful matter”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038041","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-40.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-42.html"},{"numVerset":42,"texteArabe":"ارْكُضْ بِرِجْلِكَ  هَاذَا مُغْتَسَلٌ بَارِدٌ وَشَرَابٌ","tradPropre":"Frappe [la terre] de ton pied: voici une eau fraîche pour te laver et voici de quoi boire.","tradEn":"[So he was told], \"Strike [the ground] with your foot; this is a [spring for a] cool bath and drink.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ce qui mettra fin à tes souffrances corporelles.","explicationUnanime":"Nous lui répondîmes: Frappe le sol de ton pied. Il s’exécuta et du sol jaillit une eau dont il but et se lava le corps. C’est alors que le mal dont il souffrait disparut.","explicationEn":"42. So I said to him: “Strike your foot on the ground”. So he struck his foot on the ground, then water sprung forth for him from it, which he would drink and bathe from and through it, his difficulty and pain would go.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038042","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-41.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-43.html"},{"numVerset":43,"texteArabe":"وَوَهَبْنَا لَهُ أَهْلَهُ وَمِثْلَهُمْ مَعَهُمْ رَحْمَةً مِنَّا وَذِكْرَىٰ لِأُولِي الْأَلْبَابِ","tradPropre":"Et Nous lui rendîmes sa famille et la fîmes deux fois plus nombreuse, comme une miséricorde de Notre part et comme un rappel pour les gens doués d'intelligence.","tradEn":"And We granted him his family and a like [number] with them as mercy from Us and a reminder for those of understanding.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous l’exauçâmes alors et fîmes disparaître le mal dont il souffrait. Puis Nous lui donnâmes une famille et doublèrent le nombre de ses enfants et petits-enfants, par miséricorde de Notre part, comme rétribution pour sa patience et afin que les gens doués d’intelligence se rappellent que les fruits de la patience sont une issue favorable et une récompense.","explicationEn":"43. So I responded to him and removed the difficulty he was affected by, and I gave him his family and added to them a like number of sons and grandsons, as a mercy from Me to him and a reward for his patience, and so that the people of superior intellect are reminded that the outcome of patience is ease and reward.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038043","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-42.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-44.html"},{"numVerset":44,"texteArabe":"وَخُذْ بِيَدِكَ ضِغْثًا فَاضْرِبْ بِهِ وَلَا تَحْنَثْ  إِنَّا وَجَدْنَاهُ صَابِرًا  نِعْمَ الْعَبْدُ  إِنَّهُ أَوَّابٌ","tradPropre":"«Et prends dans ta main un faisceau de brindilles, puis frappe avec cela. Et ne viole pas ton serment». Oui, Nous l'avons trouvé vraiment endurant. Quel bon serviteur! Sans cesse il se repentait.","tradEn":"[We said], \"And take in your hand a bunch [of grass] and strike with it and do not break your oath.\" Indeed, We found him patient, an excellent servant. Indeed, he was one repeatedly turning back [to Allāh].","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> S’étant un jour emporté contre celle-ci lors de sa maladie, Job aurait juré de lui infliger cent coups de fouet s’il guérissait (Tafsîr ibn Kathîr).","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque Job fut en colère contre son épouse, il fit le serment qu’il allait lui infliger cent coups de fouet mais Nous lui dîmes: Ô Job, prends un faisceau de brindilles et frappe-la avec, afin de ne pas commettre de parjure. Il obéit et Nous le trouvâmes patient dans l’épreuve que Nous lui avons fait subir. Quel bon serviteur qui se repentait souvent à Allah.","explicationEn":"44. When Job became angry with his wife, he swore an oath he will lash her a hundred times, so I said to him: “O Job, take a bunch of stalks in your hand and hit her with them, to fulfil your oath. And do not break the oath you made”. So he took a bunch of stalks and hit her with them. I found him to be patient in what I afflicted him with. What an excellent servant he was. He would turn to Allah abundantly.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038044","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-43.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-45.html"},{"numVerset":45,"texteArabe":"وَاذْكُرْ عِبَادَنَا إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَإِسْحَاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ أُولِي الْأَيْدِي وَالْأَبْصَارِ","tradPropre":"Et rappelle-toi Abraham, Isaac et Jacob, Nos serviteurs puissants et clairvoyants.","tradEn":"And remember Our servants, Abraham, Isaac and Jacob - those of strength and [religious] vision.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, rappelle-toi de Nos serviteurs que Nous avons élus et de Nos messagers que Nous avons envoyés: Abraham, Isaac et Jacob. Ils étaient doués de force dans leur obéissance à Allah et la recherche de Son agrément. Ils étaient également dotés d’une sincère clairvoyance qui leur faisait suivre la vérité.","explicationEn":"45. O Messenger, remember My servants I chose and the messengers I sent: Abraham, Isaac and Jacob. They were people of strength in Allah’s obedience and seeking His pleasure, and they were people of true insight into the truth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038045","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-44.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-46.html"},{"numVerset":46,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا أَخْلَصْنَاهُمْ بِخَالِصَةٍ ذِكْرَى الدَّارِ","tradPropre":"Nous avons fait d'eux l'objet d'une distinction particulière: le rappel de l'au-delà.","tradEn":"Indeed, We chose them for an exclusive quality: remembrance of the home [of the Hereafter].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous leur avons fait la faveur spécifique d’emplir leur cœur du rappel de l’au-delà et de les préparer à rejoindre cette demeure en accomplissant de bonnes œuvres et en appelant les gens à en accomplir.","explicationEn":"46. I favoured them with a special favour I chose them with, which was filling their hearts with the remembrance of the abode of the Afterlife, preparing for it through good actions and calling people towards acting for it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038046","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-45.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-47.html"},{"numVerset":47,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّهُمْ عِنْدَنَا لَمِنَ الْمُصْطَفَيْنَ الْأَخْيَارِ","tradPropre":"Ils sont auprès de Nous, certes, parmi les meilleurs élus.","tradEn":"And indeed they are, to Us, among the chosen and outstanding.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pour Nous, ils sont du nombre de ceux que Nous avons élus pour Nous obéir et Nous adorer. Nous les avons, en effet, choisis afin qu’ils portent Notre Message et le transmettent aux gens.","explicationEn":"47. And they were with Me amongst those I chose for My obedience and worship, and whom I selected to bear My message and convey it to the people.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038047","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-46.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-48.html"},{"numVerset":48,"texteArabe":"وَاذْكُرْ إِسْمَاعِيلَ وَالْيَسَعَ وَذَا الْكِفْلِ  وَكُلٌّ مِنَ الْأَخْيَارِ","tradPropre":"Et rappelle-toi Ismaël et Elisée, et Dal Kifl, chacun d'eux parmi les meilleurs.","tradEn":"And remember Ishmael, Elisha and Dhul-Kifl, and all are among the outstanding.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, rappelle-toi d’Ismaël fils d’Abraham, d’Elisée (Alyasa’), de Dhû al-Kifl et fais leur éloge car ils le méritent. Tous ont été élus et choisis par Allah","explicationEn":"48. O Prophet, remember Ishmael, the son of Abraham, and remember Elisha, and remember Dhul-Kifl, and praise them well as they deserve it. And all of these were amongst the chosen and selected in Allah’s sight.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038048","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-47.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-49.html"},{"numVerset":49,"texteArabe":"هَاذَا ذِكْرٌ  وَإِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ لَحُسْنَ مَآبٍ","tradPropre":"Cela est un rappel. C'est aux pieux qu'appartient, en vérité, la meilleure retraite,","tradEn":"This is a reminder. And indeed, for the righteous is a good place of return -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceci est une mention élogieuse de ces hommes dans le Coran et ceux qui craignent Allah en se conformant à Ses commandements et en renonçant à Ses interdits, connaîtront un retour favorable dans l’au-delà.","explicationEn":"49. This is a reminder of these people through good praise in the Qur’ān. And for the Mindful through carrying out the orders of Allah and refraining from His prohibitions is a good return in the abode of the Afterlife.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038049","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-48.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-50.html"},{"numVerset":50,"texteArabe":"جَنَّاتِ عَدْنٍ مُفَتَّحَةً لَهُمُ الْأَبْوَابُ","tradPropre":"Les Jardins d'Eden, aux portes ouvertes pour eux,","tradEn":"Gardens of perpetual residence, whose doors will be opened to them.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils iront le Jour de la Résurrection dans des vergers pour y demeurer et on leur ouvrira leurs portes afin de les accueillir.","explicationEn":"50. This good return is gardens of residence they will enter on the Day of Judgment, whose doors will be opened to welcome them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038050","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-49.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-51.html"},{"numVerset":51,"texteArabe":"مُتَّكِئِينَ فِيهَا يَدْعُونَ فِيهَا بِفَاكِهَةٍ كَثِيرَةٍ وَشَرَابٍ","tradPropre":"où, accoudés, ils demanderont des fruits abondants et des boissons.","tradEn":"Reclining within them, they will call therein for abundant fruit and drink.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils y seront accoudés à des banquettes qui auront été ornées pour eux et ils ordonneront à leurs serviteurs de leur présenter les variétés de fruits et de boissons, vin ou autre, qu’ils désirent.","explicationEn":"51. Reclining on couches which will be adorned for them. They will ask their attendants to present to them the many different types of fruit they will desire and the drinks they will desire, such as wine and so forth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038051","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-50.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-52.html"},{"numVerset":52,"texteArabe":"۞ وَعِنْدَهُمْ قَاصِرَاتُ الطَّرْفِ أَتْرَابٌ","tradPropre":"Et auprès d'eux seront les belles au regard chaste, toutes du même âge.","tradEn":"And with them will be women limiting [their] glances and of equal age.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il y aura auprès d’eux des femmes d’un âge moyen qui ne regarderont que leurs époux et personne d’autre.","explicationEn":"52. And with them will be women, all of similar age, whose gaze will be limited only to their husbands.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038052","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-51.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-53.html"},{"numVerset":53,"texteArabe":"هَاذَا مَا تُوعَدُونَ لِيَوْمِ الْحِسَابِ","tradPropre":"Voilà ce qui vous est promis pour le Jour des Comptes.","tradEn":"This is what you, [the righteous], are promised for the Day of Account.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens pieux, voilà la rétribution agréable que l’on vous promet le Jour de la Résurrection pour les bonnes œuvres que vous accomplissiez dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"53. O Alah-conscious people, this is the pleasant reward you are being promised on the day of judgment for your good deeds you used to do in the world.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038053","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-52.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-54.html"},{"numVerset":54,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ هَاذَا لَرِزْقُنَا مَا لَهُ مِنْ نَفَادٍ","tradPropre":"Ce sera Notre attribution inépuisable.","tradEn":"Indeed, this is Our provision; for it there is no depletion.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce que Nous avons mentionné est la rétribution dont Nous pourvoirons les serviteurs pieux le Jour de la Résurrection. Ce sera un don continu qui ne s’interrompra jamais","explicationEn":"54. This reward I have mentioned is My provision I will give to the Alah-conscious on the Day of Judgment, and it is continuous provision which will not pause or end.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038054","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-53.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-55.html"},{"numVerset":55,"texteArabe":"هَاذَا  وَإِنَّ لِلطَّاغِينَ لَشَرَّ مَآبٍ","tradPropre":"Voilà! Alors que les rebelles auront certes la pire retraite,","tradEn":"This [is so]. But indeed, for the transgressors is an evil place of return -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceci est en effet la rétribution des gens pieux, tandis que ceux qui outrepassent les limites d’Allah en mécroyant et en commettant des péchés auront droit à une rétribution totalement opposée: leur retour sera le pire qui soit le Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"55. This that I mentioned is the reward of the Mindful. And those who trespass the limits of Allah through disbelief and sins will have a reward different to that of the Mindful, so for them is a bad return they shall return to on the day of judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038055","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-54.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-56.html"},{"numVerset":56,"texteArabe":"جَهَنَّمَ يَصْلَوْنَهَا فَبِئْسَ الْمِهَادُ","tradPropre":"L'Enfer où ils brûleront. Et quel affreux lit!","tradEn":"Hell, which they will [enter to] burn, and wretched is the resting place.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils iront en Enfer qui les cernera de toutes parts et ils endureront sa chaleur et ses flammes. Il sera leur literie et quelle pire literie que l’Enfer.","explicationEn":"56. This reward is hell which will surround them, and they will suffer its heat and flames. From it they will have a spread, so what an evil spread is theirs.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038056","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-55.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-57.html"},{"numVerset":57,"texteArabe":"هَاذَا فَلْيَذُوقُوهُ حَمِيمٌ وَغَسَّاقٌ","tradPropre":"Voilà! Qu'ils y goûtent: eau bouillante et eau purulente,","tradEn":"This - so let them taste it - is scalding water and [foul] purulence.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Leur supplice consistera à boire une eau extrêmement brûlante et du pus s’écoulant des corps des suppliciés en Enfer. Qu’ils boivent de ces boissons qui n’étancheront jamais leur soif.","explicationEn":"57. This punishment is extremely hot water, and pus which will flow from the bodies of the people of hell being punished in it, so they should taste it as it is their drink. However it is a drink which does not quench thirst.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038057","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-56.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-58.html"},{"numVerset":58,"texteArabe":"وَآخَرُ مِنْ شَكْلِهِ أَزْوَاجٌ","tradPropre":"et d'autres punitions du même genre.","tradEn":"And other [punishments] of its type [in various] kinds.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils subiront d’autres supplices du même genre et d’autres complètement différents.","explicationEn":"58. And they will have another punishment like this punishment. They will have a number of various punishments they will be punished with in the Afterlife.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038058","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-57.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-59.html"},{"numVerset":59,"texteArabe":"هَاذَا فَوْجٌ مُقْتَحِمٌ مَعَكُمْ  لَا مَرْحَبًا بِهِمْ  إِنَّهُمْ صَالُو النَّارِ","tradPropre":"Voici un groupe qui entre précipitamment en même temps que vous, nulle bienvenue à eux. Ils vont brûler dans le Feu.","tradEn":"[Its inhabitants will say], \"This is a company bursting in with you. No welcome for them. Indeed, they will burn in the Fire.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Diront les chefs de l’impiété en Enfer, selon nombre d’exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque les gens de l’Enfer entreront en Enfer, des disputes éclateront entre eux. Ils s’invectiveront les uns les autres et les uns se désavoueront des autres. Certains diront: Voici un groupe qui entrera en Enfer avec vous. Les autres répondront: Qu’ils ne soient pas les bienvenus car ils endureront le feu que nous endurons.","explicationEn":"59. And when the people of hellfire will enter, they will dispute with one another, cursing and disassociating from one another. When it will be said to those already in the fire: “This is a new group of those that will inhabit the fire with you, they will respond:” “May they not be welcome, they will suffer the punishment like we are suffering”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038059","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-58.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-60.html"},{"numVerset":60,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا بَلْ أَنْتُمْ لَا مَرْحَبًا بِكُمْ  أَنْتُمْ قَدَّمْتُمُوهُ لَنَا  فَبِئْسَ الْقَرَارُ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Pas de bienvenue pour vous, plutôt. C'est vous qui avez préparé cela pour nous». Quel mauvais lieu de séjour!","tradEn":"They will say, \"Nor you! No welcome for you. You, [our leaders], brought this upon us, and wretched is the settlement.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les suiveurs diront à leurs chefs meneurs: Ô chefs meneurs, c’est plutôt vous qui n’êtes pas les bienvenus car c’est vous qui êtes la cause du châtiment douloureux que nous subissons car vous nous avez égarés et nous avez trompés. Que la demeure, l’Enfer, de tous ces gens est mauvaise.","explicationEn":"60. The group of followers will say to their leaders who were followed: “But rather you, O leaders who were followed, no welcome to you, as you are what caused us this painful punishment by misguiding us and leading us astray”. What a terrible settlement this is, the settlement of hell fire for them all.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038060","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-59.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-61.html"},{"numVerset":61,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا رَبَّنَا مَنْ قَدَّمَ لَنَا هَاذَا فَزِدْهُ عَذَابًا ضِعْفًا فِي النَّارِ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Seigneur, celui qui nous a préparé cela, ajoute-lui un double châtiment dans le Feu».","tradEn":"They will say, \"Our Lord, whoever brought this upon us - increase for him double punishment in the Fire.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les suiveurs diront: Ô notre Seigneur, double le châtiment de ceux qui nous ont détournés de la guidée lorsque celle-ci nous est parvenue.","explicationEn":"61. The followers will say: “Our Lord, whoever lead us astray from the guidance after it came to us, double his punishment in the fire”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038061","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-60.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-62.html"},{"numVerset":62,"texteArabe":"وَقَالُوا مَا لَنَا لَا نَرَىٰ رِجَالًا كُنَّا نَعُدُّهُمْ مِنَ الْأَشْرَارِ","tradPropre":"Et ils dirent: «Pourquoi ne voyons-nous pas des gens que nous comptions parmi les malfaiteurs?","tradEn":"And they will say, \"Why do we not see men whom we used to count among the worst?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les arrogants et les tyrans diront: Pourquoi ne voyons-nous pas dans le feu, des hommes que nous considérions dans le bas monde comme des misérables qui méritent le châtiment.","explicationEn":"62. And the arrogant transgressors will say: “Why do we not see with us in the fire men we used to consider in the world amongst the wretched who deserved punishment?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038062","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-61.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-63.html"},{"numVerset":63,"texteArabe":"أَتَّخَذْنَاهُمْ سِخْرِيًّا أَمْ زَاغَتْ عَنْهُمُ الْأَبْصَارُ","tradPropre":"Est-ce que nous les avons raillés (à tort) ou échappent-ils à nos regards?»","tradEn":"Is it [because] we took them in ridicule, or has [our] vision turned away from them?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous sommes-nous trompés lorsque nous les avons raillés alors qu’il s’avère qu’ils ne méritent pas d’être châtiés? Ou alors avions-nous raison et ils sont bien entrés en Enfer sans que nous ne les ayons vus?","explicationEn":"63. Was our mocking them a mistake and so they did not deserve to be punished, or was our mocking them right, and they have entered the fire but we have not seen them yet?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038063","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-62.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-64.html"},{"numVerset":64,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ ذَالِكَ لَحَقٌّ تَخَاصُمُ أَهْلِ النَّارِ","tradPropre":"Telles sont en vérité les querelles des gens du Feu.","tradEn":"Indeed, that is truth [i.e., reality] - the quarreling of the people of the Fire.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les disputes entre mécréants qui sont décrites ici et qui auront lieu le Jour de la Résurrection sont une vérité indubitable.","explicationEn":"64. This which has been mentioned to you, namely the arguments of the disbelievers on the Day of Judgment, is the truth in which there is no dispute or doubt.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038064","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-63.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-65.html"},{"numVerset":65,"texteArabe":"قُلْ إِنَّمَا أَنَا مُنْذِرٌ  وَمَا مِنْ إِلَاهٍ إِلَّا اللَّهُ الْوَاحِدُ الْقَهَّارُ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Je ne suis qu'un avertisseur. Point de divinité à part Allah, l'Unique, le Dominateur Suprême,","tradEn":"Say, [O Muḥammad], \"I am only a warner, and there is not any deity except Allāh, the One, the Prevailing,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Muħammad, dis aux mécréants de ton peuple: Je ne fais que vous avertir contre le châtiment qu’Allah abattra sur vous pour votre mécréance et le démenti que vous opposiez à Ses messagers. Il n’existe pas de dieu méritant d’être adoré hormis Allah. Il est Unique dans Son éminence, Ses attributs et Ses noms. Il est le Dominateur qui domine tout et tout Lui est soumis.","explicationEn":"65. O Muhammad, say to the disbelievers from your people: “I am only a warner to you of Allah’s punishment, lest it fall upon you due to disbelief and denying His messengers. And there is no god who deserves to be worshipped besides Allah, as He is unique in His greatness, qualities and names, and He is the Subduer who has subdued everything. So everything submits to Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038065","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-64.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-66.html"},{"numVerset":66,"texteArabe":"رَبُّ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا الْعَزِيزُ الْغَفَّارُ","tradPropre":"Seigneur des cieux et de la terre et de ce qui existe entre eux, le Puissant, le Grand Pardonneur».","tradEn":"Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them, the Exalted in Might, the Perpetual Forgiver.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il est le Seigneur des Cieux, de la Terre et de ce qui se trouve entre les deux. Il est le Puissant dans Son Royaume, où personne ne Lui tient tête, et Il pardonne les péchés de Ses serviteurs qui se repentent.","explicationEn":"66. And He is the Lord of the heavens, the Lord of the earth and Lord of whatever is in between them. And He is Mighty in His kingdom, with nobody to overpower Him, and He is Forgiving of the sins of His servants who repent to Him”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038066","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-65.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-67.html"},{"numVerset":67,"texteArabe":"قُلْ هُوَ نَبَأٌ عَظِيمٌ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Ceci (le Coran) est une grande nouvelle,","tradEn":"Say, \"It is great news","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis à ces dénégateurs: Le Coran est une nouvelle d’une importance suprême.","explicationEn":"67. O Messenger, say to these deniers: “The Qur’ān is a news of great status.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038067","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-66.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-68.html"},{"numVerset":68,"texteArabe":"أَنْتُمْ عَنْهُ مُعْرِضُونَ","tradPropre":"mais vous vous en détournez.","tradEn":"From which you turn away.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Mais vous vous en détournez et ne lui accordez pas d’importance.","explicationEn":"68. You are turning away from this news of great status; you do not turn towards it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038068","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-67.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-69.html"},{"numVerset":69,"texteArabe":"مَا كَانَ لِيَ مِنْ عِلْمٍ بِالْمَلَإِ الْأَعْلَىٰ إِذْ يَخْتَصِمُونَ","tradPropre":"Je n'avais aucune connaissance de la cohorte sublime au moment où elle disputait.","tradEn":"I had no knowledge of the exalted assembly [of angels] when they were disputing [the creation of Adam].","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Les anges et Satan qui s’opposèrent au sujet d’Adam, comme le montrera la fin de la sourate.<br><br><strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Avant de recevoir la Révélation.","explicationUnanime":"Je n’ai aucune connaissance de ce que disent les anges au sujet de la création d'Adam, si ce n’est qu’Allah a fait descendre sur moi la Révélation et m’a instruit.","explicationEn":"69. I do not have knowledge of the discussion between the angels regarding the creation of Adam, if Allah had not revealed to me and taught me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038069","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-68.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-70.html"},{"numVerset":70,"texteArabe":"إِنْ يُوحَىٰ إِلَيَّ إِلَّا أَنَّمَا أَنَا نَذِيرٌ مُبِينٌ","tradPropre":"Il m'est seulement révélé que je suis un avertisseur clair».","tradEn":"It has not been revealed to me except that I am a clear warner.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah ne me révèle ce qu’Il me révèle que pour vous avertir clairement de Son châtiment.","explicationEn":"70. Allah only reveals to me what He reveals, and I am a clear warner to you of His punishment”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038070","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-69.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-71.html"},{"numVerset":71,"texteArabe":"إِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ إِنِّي خَالِقٌ بَشَرًا مِنْ طِينٍ","tradPropre":"Quand ton Seigneur dit aux Anges: «Je vais créer d'argile un être humain.","tradEn":"[So mention] when your Lord said to the angels, \"Indeed, I am going to create a human being from clay.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Rappelle-toi lorsque ton Seigneur dit aux anges: Je vais créer un être humain à partir d’argile. Il s’agit d’Adam.","explicationEn":"71. Remember when your Lord said to the angels: “I am going to create a man from clay, and he is Adam (peace be upon him).","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038071","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-70.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-72.html"},{"numVerset":72,"texteArabe":"فَإِذَا سَوَّيْتُهُ وَنَفَخْتُ فِيهِ مِنْ رُوحِي فَقَعُوا لَهُ سَاجِدِينَ","tradPropre":"Quand Je l'aurai bien formé et lui aurai insufflé de Mon Esprit, jetez-vous devant lui, prosternés».","tradEn":"So when I have proportioned him and breathed into him of My [created] soul, then fall down to him in prostration.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque J’aurai achevé sa création, l’aurai bien formé et lui aurai insufflé de Mon Esprit, prosternez-vous devant lui.","explicationEn":"72. So once I have proportioned his form, made his appearance right and blown My spirit into him, prostrate to him”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038072","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-71.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-73.html"},{"numVerset":73,"texteArabe":"فَسَجَدَ الْمَلَائِكَةُ كُلُّهُمْ أَجْمَعُونَ","tradPropre":"Alors tous les Anges se prosternèrent,","tradEn":"So the angels prostrated - all of them entirely,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les anges obéirent tous sans exception à l’ordre de leur Seigneur et se prosternèrent en guise de respect à Adam.","explicationEn":"73. So the angels obeyed the command of their Lord, so all of them prostrated by way of greeting and honour, and none of them remained except that they prostrated to Adam.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038073","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-72.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-74.html"},{"numVerset":74,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا إِبْلِيسَ اسْتَكْبَرَ وَكَانَ مِنَ الْكَافِرِينَ","tradPropre":"à l'exception d'Iblîs qui s'enfla d'orgueil et fut du nombre des infidèles.","tradEn":"Except Iblees; he was arrogant and became among the disbelievers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Seul Iblîs dédaigna se prosterner et pour cette raison il devint mécréant.","explicationEn":"74. Besides Iblis who was too arrogant to prostrate. And through his being arrogant to the command of his Lord, he was from the disbelievers.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038074","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-73.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-75.html"},{"numVerset":75,"texteArabe":"قَالَ يَا إِبْلِيسُ مَا مَنَعَكَ أَنْ تَسْجُدَ لِمَا خَلَقْتُ بِيَدَيَّ  أَسْتَكْبَرْتَ أَمْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الْعَالِينَ","tradPropre":"(Allah) lui dit: «O Iblîs, qui t'a empêché de te prosterner devant ce que J'ai créé de Mes mains? T'enfles-tu d'orgueil ou te considères-tu parmi les hauts placés?»","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"O Iblees, what prevented you from prostrating to that which I created with My hands? Were you arrogant [then], or were you [already] among the haughty?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah dit: Ô Iblîs, que t’a empêché de te prosterner devant Adam que J’ai créé de Mes mains? Est-ce de l’orgueil, te montrais-tu auparavant orgueilleux à l’égard de ton Seigneur?","explicationEn":"75. Allah said: “O Iblis, what stopped you from prostrating to Adam whom I created with My hands? Did pride stop you from prostrating or were you arrogant and haughty over your Lord from before?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038075","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-74.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-76.html"},{"numVerset":76,"texteArabe":"قَالَ أَنَا خَيْرٌ مِنْهُ  خَلَقْتَنِي مِنْ نَارٍ وَخَلَقْتَهُ مِنْ طِينٍ","tradPropre":"«Je suis meilleur que lui, dit [Iblîs,] Tu m'as créé de feu et tu l'as créé d'argile».","tradEn":"He said, \"I am better than him. You created me from fire and created him from clay.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Iblîs répondit: Je suis meilleur qu’Adam car Tu m’as créé de feu alors que lui, Tu l’as créé d’argile. Iblîs prétendait ainsi que le feu est un élément plus noble que l’argile.","explicationEn":"76. Iblis said: “I am better than Adam. You created me from fire and you created him from clay. And fire is a more noble substance than clay”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038076","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-75.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-77.html"},{"numVerset":77,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَاخْرُجْ مِنْهَا فَإِنَّكَ رَجِيمٌ","tradPropre":"(Allah) dit: «Sors d'ici, te voilà banni;","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"Then get out of it [i.e., Paradise], for indeed, you are expelled.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah dit à Iblîs: Sors du Paradis maudit et honni.","explicationEn":"77. Allah said to Iblis: “Get out of Paradise, because you are accursed and reviled.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038077","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-76.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-78.html"},{"numVerset":78,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ عَلَيْكَ لَعْنَتِي إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ","tradPropre":"et sur toi sera ma malédiction jusqu'au jour de la Rétribution».","tradEn":"And indeed, upon you is My curse until the Day of Recompense.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tu seras chassé du Paradis jusqu’au Jour de la Rétribution qui est le Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"78. And you are to be rejected from Paradise until the day of recompense, which is the day of judgment”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038078","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-77.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-79.html"},{"numVerset":79,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبِّ فَأَنْظِرْنِي إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ","tradPropre":"«Seigneur, dit [Iblîs], donne-moi donc un délai, jusqu'au jour où ils seront ressuscités».","tradEn":"He said, \"My Lord, then reprieve me until the Day they are resurrected.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Iblîs demanda ensuite à Allah: Accorde-moi un délai et ne me fais pas mourir jusqu’au jour où Tu ressusciteras Tes serviteurs.","explicationEn":"79. Iblis said: “Give me respite and do not make me die until the day You raise Your servants”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038079","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-78.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-80.html"},{"numVerset":80,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَإِنَّكَ مِنَ الْمُنْظَرِينَ","tradPropre":"(Allah) dit: «Tu es de ceux à qui un délai est accordé,","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"So indeed, you are of those reprieved","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah lui répondit: Ce délai t’est accordé.","explicationEn":"80. Allah said: “You are amongst those given respite.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038080","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-79.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-81.html"},{"numVerset":81,"texteArabe":"إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ الْوَقْتِ الْمَعْلُومِ","tradPropre":"jusqu'au jour de l'Instant bien Connu».","tradEn":"Until the Day of the time well-known.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ton délai s’étendra jusqu’au jour de l’instant bien connu où tu connaîtras la mort.","explicationEn":"81. Until the day of the known time which is fixed for your destruction”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038081","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-80.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-82.html"},{"numVerset":82,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَبِعِزَّتِكَ لَأُغْوِيَنَّهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ","tradPropre":"«Par Ta puissance! dit [Satan]. Je les séduirai assurément tous,","tradEn":"[Iblees] said, \"By Your might, I will surely mislead them all","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Iblîs dit: Je fais le serment par Ton pouvoir et Ta domination que j’égarerai tous les descendants d’Adam.","explicationEn":"82. Iblis said: “I swear by Your power and domination that I shall misguide all of the children of Adam.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038082","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-81.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-83.html"},{"numVerset":83,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا عِبَادَكَ مِنْهُمُ الْمُخْلَصِينَ","tradPropre":"sauf Tes serviteurs élus parmi eux».","tradEn":"Except, among them, Your chosen servants.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Excepté ceux que Tu auras préservés de mon égarement et que Tu as élus afin qu’ils T’adorent Seul.","explicationEn":"83. Except whom You protect from my misguiding and You have chosen to worship You alone”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038083","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-82.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-84.html"},{"numVerset":84,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَالْحَقُّ وَالْحَقَّ أَقُولُ","tradPropre":"(Allah) dit: «En vérité, et c'est la vérité que je dis,","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"The truth [is My oath], and the truth I say -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah dit: La vérité provient de Moi et Je dis la vérité, rien d’autre que la vérité.","explicationEn":"84. Allah said: “The truth is from Me and the truth is what I say. I do not say anything besides it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038084","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-83.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-85.html"},{"numVerset":85,"texteArabe":"لَأَمْلَأَنَّ جَهَنَّمَ مِنْكَ وَمِمَّنْ تَبِعَكَ مِنْهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ","tradPropre":"J'emplirai certainement l'Enfer de toi et de tous ceux d'entre eux qui te suivront».","tradEn":"[That] I will surely fill Hell with you and those of them that follow you all together.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Jour de la Résurrection, J’emplirai l’Enfer de toi et de tous les descendants d’Adam qui t’auront suivi dans la mécréance.","explicationEn":"85. On the Day of Judgment, I shall fill hell with you and your children, O Iblis, and those from the children of Adam who follow you in your disbelief, all of you”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038085","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-84.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-86.html"},{"numVerset":86,"texteArabe":"قُلْ مَا أَسْأَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ أَجْرٍ وَمَا أَنَا مِنَ الْمُتَكَلِّفِينَ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Pour cela, je ne vous demande aucun salaire; et je ne suis pas un imposteur.","tradEn":"Say, [O Muḥammad], \"I do not ask you for it [i.e., the Qur’ān] any payment, and I am not of the pretentious.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis à ces polythéistes: Je ne vous demande aucune rétribution pour les bons conseils que je vous transmets et je ne me permets pas d’ajouter à ce qui m’a été ordonné de transmettre","explicationEn":"86. Say - O Messenger, to these idolaters: “I do not ask you for any reward for the advice I convey to you, and I am not of the pretentious by bringing more than what I have been ordered with.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038086","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-85.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-87.html"},{"numVerset":87,"texteArabe":"إِنْ هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِلْعَالَمِينَ","tradPropre":"Ceci [le Coran] n'est qu'un rappel à l'univers.","tradEn":"It is but a reminder to the worlds.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Coran n’est qu’un rappel adressé aux humains et aux djinns juridiquement aptes [à assumer les charges de la religion].","explicationEn":"87. The Qur’ān is only a reminder to those who are accountable amongst men and jinns.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038087","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-86.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-88.html"},{"numVerset":88,"texteArabe":"وَلَتَعْلَمُنَّ نَبَأَهُ بَعْدَ حِينٍ","tradPropre":"Et certainement vous en aurez des nouvelles bientôt!»","tradEn":"And you will surely know [the truth of] its information after a time.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Vous vérifierez certainement la véracité de ce Coran dans peu de temps lorsque vous mourrez.","explicationEn":"88. And you will come to know the news of this Qur’ān and that it is true, after a short time when you die”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"038088","lienPrecedent":"sourate-38-verset-87.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-39-verset-1.html"}]};